.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt MSCRIPT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mscript
.Nd VBScript-compatible interpreter
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl e Ar code | Ar script.vbs Op Ar args ...
.Nm
.Fl v | Fl Fl version
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl Fl help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a tree-walking interpreter for the VBScript language, written in C++23 and
built with the system Clang compiler.
It executes
.Pa .vbs
scripts directly, without WSH/cscript.
.Pp
The interpreter implements Variant semantics (Empty, Null, Boolean, Integer,
Long, Double, Date, String, arrays and objects), the full VBScript operator
set, all standard control-flow constructs, procedures with
.Ar ByVal/ByRef
parameters, classes, error handling via
.Dv On Error
and the
.Dv Err
object, and the usual built-in functions (string, math, date/time,
conversion).
Host objects include
.Dv WScript ,
.Dv Err ,
and
.Fn CreateObject
targets
.Qq Scripting.Dictionary ,
.Qq Scripting.FileSystemObject ,
.Qq WScript.Shell ,
.Qq WScript.Network ,
.Qq ADODB.Stream
(in-memory text/binary streams with
.Dv LoadFromFile
and
.Dv SaveToFile ) ,
and any
.Qq MSXML Ns Ar 2/3/4/6 . Ns Qq DOMDocument
(progIDs such as
.Qq MSXML2.DOMDocument.6.0 ,
parsed with the system bsdxml (expat 2) library; supports
.Dv load ,
.Dv loadXML ,
.Dv save ,
.Dv documentElement ,
.Dv parseError ,
node traversal and attributes,
.Dv selectNodes /
.Dv selectSingleNode
with an XPath subset, and document construction via
.Dv createElement
and
.Dv appendChild ) ,
and any
.Qq MSXML Ns Ar 2/3/4/6 . Ns Qq XMLHTTP
(progIDs such as
.Qq MSXML2.XMLHTTP.6.0 ,
.Qq MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP ,
.Qq Microsoft.XMLHTTP ;
.Dv open ,
.Dv send ,
.Dv setRequestHeader ,
.Dv abort ,
.Dv getAllResponseHeaders ,
.Dv getResponseHeader ,
with properties
.Dv readyState ,
.Dv status ,
.Dv statusText ,
.Dv responseText ,
.Dv responseBody ,
.Dv responseXML ,
.Dv timeout .
.Pp
.Dv http://
requests use a built-in HTTP/1.1 client (status line, response headers,
chunked transfer decoding, redirect following, custom request headers);
.Dv https://
and
.Dv file://
requests go through the system libfetch library, which provides TLS for
.Dv https:// ) ,
.Qq WinHttp.WinHttpRequest.5.1
(same transport, plus the WinHTTP-specific
.Dv Option
parameterized property — 0 UserAgentString, 1 URL (read-only), 6
EnableRedirects, 14 MaxAutomaticRedirects —
.Dv SetTimeouts ,
.Dv WaitForResponse
and
.Dv SetCredentials ;
.Dv SetProxy
and
.Dv SetClientCertificate
are accepted no-ops), and
.Qq VBScript.RegExp
(built on the libc POSIX regex,
.Fn regcomp / regexec :
.Dv Pattern ,
.Dv Global ,
.Dv IgnoreCase ,
.Dv Multiline ,
.Dv Test ,
.Dv Execute ,
.Dv Replace ,
with
.Dv Match
objects
.Pq Dv FirstIndex , Dv Length , Dv Value , Dv SubMatches
and match collections supporting
.Dv Count ,
.Dv Item(i)
and
.Dv For Each ) , and
.Qq ADODB.Connection ,
.Qq ADODB.Recordset
and
.Qq ADODB.Command
backed by SQLite3, the database library in the base system
(connection strings
.Qq Provider=SQLite3;Data Source=file.db ,
a bare path or
.Qq :memory: ;
only the SQLite3 provider is supported;
.Dv Mode
.Dv adModeRead
opens read-only).
Recordsets support
.Dv Execute ,
.Dv MoveFirst/Last/Next/Previous/Move ,
.Dv AbsolutePosition ,
.Dv RecordCount ,
.Dv BOF/EF ,
.Dv Fields
(with
.Dv Count ,
.Dv Item(i) ,
.Dv For Each
and field
.Dv Name/Value/Type ) ,
.Dv GetRows ,
.Dv GetString ,
.Dv AddNew/Update/Delete/CancelUpdate
(writes require a simple single-table
.Dv SELECT ;
other sources are read-only),
and transactions
.Dv BeginTrans/CommitTrans/RollbackTrans
(nested via savepoints).
.Dv Command
supports
.Dv CommandText ,
.Dv CommandType
.Pq Dv adCmdText / adCmdTable ) ,
.Dv CreateParameter
and positional
.Pq Dv ? )
or named
.Pq Dv :name )
parameter binding.
.Pp
When the script is given as
.Qq - ,
source is read from standard input.
Arguments following the script name are available to the script through
.Dv WScript.Arguments .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl e , Fl Fl eval Ar code
Execute
.Ar code
instead of a script file.
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.It Fl v , Fl Fl version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev WSCRIPT_PATH
Reported by
.Dv WScript.Path
when set (defaults to
.Qq / ) .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/mscript
The interpreter binary.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/man/man1/mscript.1
This manual page.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std mscript
Normally, the exit status is 0.
If the script calls
.Dv WScript.Quit ,
the given code is used.
A usage error exits with 2.
A syntax error or an unhandled VBScript runtime error exits with 1 and prints
a diagnostic of the form:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mscript: script.vbs(12): Microsoft VBScript runtime error
    '800a0009': Subscript out of range
.Ed
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run a script file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ mscript hello.vbs
Hello, World!
.Ed
.Pp
Run code from the command line:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ mscript -e 'WScript.Echo 6 * 7'
42
.Ed
.Pp
Read a script from standard input:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ echo 'WScript.Echo "hi"' | mscript -
hi
.Ed
.Pp
A larger example ships in
.Pa examples/demo.vbs
(a word-frequency report using
.Qq Scripting.Dictionary ,
.Qq Scripting.FileSystemObject ,
classes and error handling).
.Sh LIMITATIONS
.Fn CreateObject
supports only the progIDs listed above; other COM objects raise error 429.
In
.Qq ADODB.Stream ,
.Dv Position
is a byte offset and
.Dv Write /
.Dv WriteText /
.Dv CopyTo
overwrite at the current position, as in ADODB.
The DOM's XPath support is the subset listed in DESCRIPTION, not full XPath 1.0;
XML names are case-sensitive.
.Dv XMLHTTP
requests are always synchronous (the
.Ar async
flag of
.Dv open
is accepted but ignored, and
.Dv onreadystatechange
is not fired, as there is no
.Dv GetRef ) .
Over
.Dv https://
and
.Dv file://
(libfetch), response headers are not exposed, so
.Dv getResponseHeader
returns an empty string and
.Dv status
is 200 on success or derived from the error reason (e.g. 404); binary request
bodies over
.Dv https://
are truncated at the first NUL byte.
Building requires the bsdxml (expat 2) library
.Pq Fl lbsdxml ) ,
libfetch
.Pq Fl lfetch ) ,
and SQLite3 from the base system
.Pq Fl lsqlite3 ;
regular expressions use the libc POSIX regex, no extra library.
.Dv ADODB
recordsets materialize the full result in memory; the
.Dv recordsAffected
out-parameter of
.Dv Execute
is not supported (host method calls do not pass
.Ar ByRef ) —
use
.Qq SELECT COUNT(*) .
Binary columns come back as byte arrays, dates bind as their serial double,
.Dv OpenSchema ,
stored procedures and the
.Dv Errors
collection are not supported.
.Dv VBScript.RegExp
translates patterns to POSIX ERE:
.Dv \ed \eD \ew \eW \es \eS ,
.Dv \en \er \et \ef \ev ,
non-capturing groups
.Pq Dv (?:... )
(group indices are remapped so
.Dv $1
and
.Dv SubMatches
count only capturing groups),
.Sq .
never matches a newline, and
.Dv Multiline
uses
.Dv REG_NEWLINE .
Backreferences
.Pq Dv \e1 ) ,
non-greedy quantifiers
.Pq Dv *? +? ?? ) ,
lookaround, named groups and
.Dv \eb
(the BSD libc regex has no word boundary) raise error 5 with a clear message.
.Dv MsgBox
prints to stdout and returns
.Dv vbOK
(no GUI);
.Dv InputBox
reads a line from standard input.
Case folding is ASCII-only.
Named arguments (:=) and GetRef are not supported.
.Dv WinHttpRequest
requests are always synchronous
.Pq Dv WaitForResponse
returns
.Dv True
immediately;
.Dv Option(6)
(EnableRedirects) is honored only on the built-in
.Dv http://
path, as libfetch always follows redirects.
